[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: backlog.SCHEMA
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[SCHEMA]
overview: Exact field layout for backlog INDEX.toon entries and items/<id>.toon detail files
principle: INDEX is scanned every time the agent engages backlog. Detail files are lazy-loaded. Schema is enforced to keep INDEX predictable and tiny.

[ID_FORMAT]
format: BL-<seq>
seq: zero-padded 3-digit integer, monotonically increasing across the whole backlog
examples: BL-001, BL-042, BL-128
never: Do not reuse IDs even after deletion. An ID always refers to the same item for the life of the repo.
next_id_rule: Read INDEX.toon, find max seq across all [ITEM.*] entries (including archived), add 1.

[INDEX_ENTRY_SHAPE]
# Exactly 7 lines per item in INDEX.toon [ITEMS] section. No extra fields here.
# Longer content belongs in items/<id>.toon.

[ITEM.BL-042]
title: <short imperative phrase, under 60 chars>
type: feature | refactor | bugfix | chore | docs
status: proposed | accepted | in-progress | done | deferred | rejected
priority: P0 | P1 | P2 | P3
created: <ISO date YYYY-MM-DD>
theme: <optional short tag for grouping; empty string if none>

# Notes on fields:
# - title: verb-phrase, not a sentence. "Add webhook retries", not "We should add retries to webhooks"
# - type: see LIFECYCLE.toon for how type affects activation (feature/refactor/bugfix route to workflow)
# - status: see LIFECYCLE.toon
# - priority: P0=urgent, P1=high, P2=normal, P3=nice-to-have. Default P2 if unspecified.
# - created: agent fills at capture time
# - theme: free-form tag, e.g. "rendering", "auth", "tech-debt". Used only for filtering; no hierarchy enforced.

[DETAIL_FILE_SHAPE]
# docs/agent/backlog/items/BL-042.toon
# Loaded ONLY when the item is being inspected, updated, or activated.

[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: backlog.item.BL-042
class: runtime-managed   # agent writes these; not tracked in manifest
version: 1.0.0

[ITEM]
id: BL-042
title: <same as index>
type: <same as index>
status: <same as index>
priority: <same as index>
created: <same as index>
theme: <same as index>

[DESCRIPTION]
# 2-6 lines: what needs to happen and why. Context enough for a future-self agent to act cold.
<prose>

[MOTIVATION]
# Why this is worth doing. What breaks or stays suboptimal if we don't.
<prose>

[ACCEPTANCE]
# Bulleted list of observable outcomes. Used as verification checklist when workflow activates this item.
- <criterion 1>
- <criterion 2>

[OUT_OF_SCOPE]
# What this item deliberately does NOT cover. Prevents scope drift on activation.
- <thing we will not do>

[LINKS]
# Optional. Any of these may be empty.
workplan: <slug if currently active, e.g. add-webhook-retries>
external_id: <e.g. AB#1234 for Azure DevOps, LIN-456 for Linear, #789 for GitHub — or empty>
epic: <path or id, e.g. docs/epics/manufacturing/EPIC-07.md#US-07-3 — or empty>
related_items: <list of BL-ids, e.g. BL-015, BL-031 — or empty>

[HISTORY]
# Append-only. One line per transition. Agent writes, never edits past entries.
<ISO datetime> — captured (proposed) — source: <user | spawn_task | workflow.REFACTOR.out_of_scope | workflow.BUGFIX.followup>
<ISO datetime> — <old status> → <new status> — <optional reason>

[INDEX_TOON_SKELETON]
# What INDEX.toon looks like when populated. Agent appends [ITEM.BL-XXX] blocks to [ITEMS].

[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: backlog.INDEX
class: parameterized
version: 1.0.0

[BACKLOG_META]
project_name: <filled at setup>
next_id_seq: <last-used + 1, kept current by agent>
last_updated: <ISO datetime>
sync_target: <none | azure-devops | linear | github>  # see SYNC.toon

[ITEMS]
# Ordered by status (in-progress → accepted → proposed → deferred → rejected → done) then by priority then by id.
# Agent re-sorts on every write.

[ITEM.BL-001]
title: ...
type: ...
status: ...
priority: ...
created: ...
theme: ...

[ITEM.BL-002]
...

[ARCHIVE]
# Optional. Once [ITEMS] exceeds ~80 entries, agent moves done/rejected items older than 30 days
# to docs/agent/backlog/archive/INDEX.toon (same schema).

[INTEGRITY_RULES]
- INDEX and detail MUST stay in sync on the six shared fields (title, type, status, priority, created, theme)
- If agent detects drift (INDEX says X, detail says Y) → detail file wins, repair INDEX, log in item HISTORY
- Never delete a detail file without also removing the INDEX entry (and vice-versa)
- Never rewrite HISTORY entries; append only
